    /// What a location's month of charging cost the site
    ///
    /// The ended sessions that **started** in the month on the location's own
    /// clock (`timeZone` says which zone, `timeZoneSource` where it came from), each
    /// whole however long it ran, priced under the location's supply contract
    /// (its own, else the project's). This is the rule `/projects/{id}/earnings`
    /// uses, not the cut `/locations/{id}/month` makes of metered energy
    /// (`sessionRule: startedInMonth`). Omit `month` for the month the location is
    /// in now.
    ///
    /// `cost` is `computed` (`currency`, `amount`: the exact sum of the sessions,
    /// VAT included when the contract has VAT) only when every ended session in the
    /// month priced. Otherwise it is the first outcome that prevented it, in the
    /// order the sessions started, and carries no amount: `noSupplyContract`,
    /// `usageUnavailable`, `pricesUnavailable` (`unpricedFrom` says where),
    /// `currencyMismatch` or `zoneUnknown`. A month with no ended session is
    /// `noSessions`. None of them is a cost of `0`. The energy is reported either
    /// way. A session still running is counted in `inProgress` and is in neither
    /// the energy nor the cost; test sessions are excluded and counted.
    ///
    /// It is priced when asked, at the contract in force now and the spot prices
    /// published for the slots the energy was drawn in (`priceBasis:
    /// currentContract`), so a figure can change between two reads and is not an
    /// invoice. A month with more sessions than one read lists is refused, never
    /// totalled over a subset.
