    /// Closes a month: from now on its figures, names and documents are fixed.
    ///
    /// Settlement builds the month from the sessions that started in it, prices
    /// them through `energy-pricing`, and stores one row per person charged plus
    /// one for the sessions nobody was tagged on, with who closed it and when. A
    /// session paid directly by card is in no row. The response is the closed
    /// month, as `GET /v1/projects/{projectId}/statements?month=` then returns it
    /// (`state.kind` is `closed`).
    ///
    /// A month closes only when every session in it has ended and every ended
    /// session is priced. `409 monthNotClosable` says so, and names the first day
    /// with energy that has no published price (`firstUnpricedDay`) when that is
    /// the reason. `409 monthAlreadyClosed` is a second close, a lost race
    /// included: exactly one of two concurrent closes succeeds.
    /// `409 monthHasOpenHolds` is a card payment in the month that has not ended
    /// (its cost is not known yet); the body says how many (`openHolds`) and since
    /// when (`openHoldsSince`, RFC 3339), and the board closes once they end.
    ///
    /// Needs the `settlement.statement.close` permission, which an `Owner` holds and
    /// the `Statements` policy grants to anyone else. An `Admin` does not hold it.
